#: ../../source/http-errors_README.md:38
msgid "Error Properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-errors_README.md:40
msgid ""
"`expose` - can be used to signal if `message` should be sent to the "
"client, defaulting to `false` when `status` >= 500"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-errors_README.md:42
msgid ""
"`headers` - can be an object of header names to values to be sent to the "
"client, defaulting to `undefined`. When defined, the key names should all"
" be lower-cased"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-errors_README.md:45
msgid ""
"`message` - the traditional error message, which should be kept short and"
" all single line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-errors_README.md:47
msgid ""
"`status` - the status code of the error, mirroring `statusCode` for "
"general compatibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-errors_README.md:49
msgid "`statusCode` - the status code of the error, defaulting to `500`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-errors_README.md:51
msgid "createError([status], [message], [properties])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-errors_README.md:53 ../../source/http-errors_README.md:99
msgid ""
"Create a new error object with the given message `msg`. The error object "
"inherits from `createError.HttpError`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-errors_README.md:60
msgid "`status: 500` - the status code as a number"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-errors_README.md:61
msgid ""
"`message` - the message of the error, defaulting to node's text for that "
"status code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-errors_README.md:62 ../../source/http-errors_README.md:87
msgid "`properties` - custom properties to attach to the object"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-errors_README.md:64
msgid "createError([status], [error], [properties])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-errors_README.md:66
msgid ""
"Extend the given `error` object with `createError.HttpError` properties. "
"This will not alter the inheritance of the given `error` object, and the "
"modified `error` object is the return value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-errors_README.md:85
msgid "`status` - the status code as a number"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-errors_README.md:86
msgid "`error` - the error object to extend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-errors_README.md:89
msgid "createError.isHttpError(val)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-errors_README.md:91
msgid ""
"Determine if the provided `val` is an `HttpError`. This will return "
"`true` if the error inherits from the `HttpError` constructor of this "
"module or matches the \"duck type\" for an error this module creates. All"
" outputs from the `createError` factory will return `true` for this "
"function, including if an non-`HttpError` was passed into the factory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/http-errors_README.md:97
msgid "new createError\\[code || name\\](\\[msg]\\))"
